# Netlify redirects for jf-commercial-readiness.
#
# THE NETLIFY URL IS NEVER REDIRECTED. It is the iframe source for
# www.jefffryer.com/commercial-readiness-audit and has to keep serving the audit
# on its own. Sending it to Squarespace would put the page inside itself.
#
# The Squarespace-side redirects are NOT configured here. They live in
# Squarespace under Settings -> Developer Tools -> URL Mappings, because that is
# the host that serves those paths. They are recorded in HANDOFF.md so the
# mapping is in version control somewhere.
#
# This file is intentionally left with no rules. It previously carried
#
#     /commercial-readiness-audit    /commercial-readiness-gap    301
#
# which pointed the wrong way: /commercial-readiness-gap is the retired page and
# /commercial-readiness-audit is the live one. It never fired, because this host
# does not serve either path, so the reversal was invisible. Anyone reading it as
# documentation would have taken the retired page for the canonical one.
